              "Categories": {
                "value": "Barack Obama in California|Photographs by Steve Jurvetson|Barack Obama in 2008|Flickr images reviewed by FlickreviewR 2|Barack Obama presidential primary campaign, 2008 in California|Barack Obama presidential campaign in April 2008",
                "source": "commons-categories",
                "hidden": ""
              },
              "Assessments": {
                "value": "",
                "source": "commons-categories",
                "hidden": ""
              },
              "ImageDescription": {
                "value": "<p>I just went through &lt;a href=\"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/jurvetson/sets/72157606812416363\">https://www.flickr.com/photos/jurvetson/sets/72157606812416363</a>\"&gt;my Obama photos&lt;/a&gt; to personalize my &lt;a href=\"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.usatoday.com/tech/news/2009-05-20-obama-time-capsule-amazon_N.htm\">https://www.usatoday.com/tech/news/2009-05-20-obama-time-capsule-amazon_N.htm</a>\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\"&gt;Time Capsule&lt;/a&gt;, and found so many that I wish I could weave in\u2026. like this sunny disposition, used for a \u201cBright Future\u201d postcard.\n</p><p>Smolan continues to push personalized book publishing from cover shots to embedded graphics and text. For example, in the Time Capsule, you can enter your own name to the inauguration invitation. I think he was trying to accommodate most buyers who have enthusiasm and art to contribute.  Hopefully the format can allow for multiple pages of user generated content\u2026 to memorialize the cultural aftertaste of a shared experience.  If variable page length binding is difficult, perhaps they could have a section of b-roll photos somewhere, and the purchaser could optionally swap out 0-10 pages of their own photos there.\n</p><p>Wish I could have included my favorite &lt;a href=\"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/jurvetson/3207520361/sizes/l\">https://www.flickr.com/photos/jurvetson/3207520361/sizes/l</a>\"&gt;inauguration celebration&lt;/a&gt; shot, and &lt;a href=\"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/jurvetson/2816735522\">https://www.flickr.com/photos/jurvetson/2816735522</a>\"&gt;thoughts&lt;/a&gt; provoked at the DNC, and &lt;a href=\"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/search/?q=obama&amp;w=44124348109@N01&amp;s=int\">https://www.flickr.com/search/?q=obama&amp;w=44124348109@N01&amp;s=int</a>\"&gt;more&lt;/a&gt;\u2026\n</p>\nAnd meanwhile, I was watching Obama\u2019s &lt;a href=\"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" data-mw-original-href=\"http://www.whitehouse.gov/blog/NewBeginning\" href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/blog/NewBeginning\">http://www.whitehouse.gov/blog/NewBeginning</a>\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\"&gt; June 4 speech&lt;/a&gt; in Cairo about America\u2019s relationship with the Muslim world.  Can you imagine Bush trying to build bridges like that? I think it\u2019s an important talk, worth viewing.",
                "source": "commons-desc-page"
              },
              "DateTimeOriginal": {
                "value": "2009-06-06 14:14",
                "source": "commons-desc-page"
              },
              "Credit": {
                "value": "<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/jurvetson/3600998291/\">Obama Postcard</a>",
